    s=json.loads((PUBLIC/'summary.json').read_text());lines=[];add=lambda value='':lines.append(value)
    add('# H3aq: safe 16-label construction still loses substantial capacity');add();add('**The prospective ≥95% capacity requirement for all eight D4-unfiltered count models is falsified: only two banks pass.** D4-unfiltered capacities range from 63.503984% to 96.538095%, versus 2.779486%–21.975396% for raw-unfiltered construction. Both unfiltered arms have zero invalid zero-F states, as their conditional safety construction predicts; that is not an independent empirical safety success. The published exposure-filtered baseline remains at 100% valid-input capacity while admitting many invalid states.');add();add('![Safety and capacity tradeoff](../../../../results/research/loki/h3aq/safety-capacity-tradeoff.png)');add()
